<protocol name="view_image" type="tool_mastery" domain="shared">

## PURPOSE

Your EYES. Returns multimodal content so you SEE images directly.
You don't get a description - you see the actual image.

---

## WHEN TO USE

| Situation | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| User provides image | view_image IMMEDIATELY |
| Before image_studio | See source, identify material/features |
| After image_studio | Verify output quality |
| Before write_data | Confirm visual attributes |

**Proactive**: When user mentions image path, VIEW IT before anything else.

---

## PARAMETERS

### image_path (required)

| Format | Example |
|--------|---------|
| Storage path | `inbox/photo.jpg`, `pending/edit.png` |
| Local path | `/path/to/image.jpg` |
| URL | `https://example.com/image.jpg` |

Storage convention:
- `inbox/` = User uploads
- `pending/` = Processed outputs

---

## WHAT YOU SEE

When you call view_image, you receive:
1. Text metadata (source, size, format)
2. The actual image in your context

Analyze:
- **Material**: Texture, transparency, finish
- **Features**: Patterns, labels, markings
- **Quality**: Lighting, clarity, condition
- **Items**: Count, positions, variations

---

## ANTI-PATTERNS

| Don't | Instead |
|-------|---------|
| Assume without viewing | View first, then act |
| Ask user to describe image | View it yourself |
| View same image repeatedly | Remember what you saw |
| Skip verification after processing | Always view output |

---

## RETURN STRUCTURE

### Success
```json
[
  {"type": "text", "text": "Image: 1024x768, JPEG"},
  {"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "data:..."}}
]
```

### Error
```json
[{"type": "text", "text": "Error: Image not found at [path]"}]
```

---

## KEY PRINCIPLE

**See before you act. See after you process.**

</protocol>
